  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-set\"><strong id=\"\">Validator sets</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>can only get so large before the messaging complexity gets in the way, causing a direct reduction in <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-do-scalability-throughput-and-tps-mean\"><strong id=\"\">throughput (TPS)</strong></a>. For the unsharded <a id=\"\" href=\"http://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radixs-babylon-mainnet\"><strong id=\"\">Babylon Mainnet</strong></a> version of the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix</strong> <strong id=\"\">Public</strong> <strong id=\"\">Network</strong></a>, a validator set of 100 provides a good compromise between redundancy and throughput.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\">In the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-radix-roadmap\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Xi’an release</strong></a>, Radix will move to a fully sharded <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">ledger</strong></a> and an effectively unlimited number of <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-validator-node-2\"><strong id=\"\">validators</strong></a>.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"http://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-throughput-tps-of-radixs-babylon-mainnet\"><strong id=\"\">What is the throughput (TPS) of Radix's Babylon Mainnet?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-are-validators-on-radix-selected\"><strong id=\"\">How are validators selected?</strong></a></li></ul><p id=\"\">‍</p>",
